  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ram Bharat vs State Of Mah. Thr. M.N. Ratnaparkhi on 1 July, 2024 Author: G. A. Sanap Bench: G. A. Sanap 2024:BHC-NAG:7113 18.cri.wp.4 1 IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY NAGPUR BENCH, NAGPUR. CRIMINAL WRIT PETITION NO. 486 OF 2023 M/s. Ram Bharat, Aged about 44 Yrs., Occupier of Patanjali Foods Limited, Having its address at Survey No. 178, Surkandi Road, Washim, Taluka District Washim // V E R S U S // 1. State of Maharashtra, Through Mr. M. N. Ratnaparkhi, Deputy Director, Industrial Safety and Health, Akola Amended as per courts 2. State of Maharashtra, order dt. 13.07.2023 Through its office at and deleted Advocates for the State of respondent Maharashtra, High Court, no.2 Nagpur ------------------------------------------------------------------- Mr. Kushal Mor alongwith Mr Apoorv Shrivastava and Mr R. R. Advocates for the petitioner Mrs H. S. Dhande, APP for respondent No.1/State ------------------------------------------------------------------- CORAM : G. A. SANAP, J. Ram Bharat vs State Of Mah. Thr. M.N. Ratnaparkhi on 1 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/153510493/ 1 DATE : 01/07/2024 ORAL JUDGMENT : 1 Heard. 18.cri.wp.486.2023judgment.odt 2 RULE. Rule made returnable forthwith. Taken up for final disposal with the consent of learned Advocates for the parties. The accident in question occurred on 16.08.2021. At about 12:30 a.m. (midnight) on 16.08.2021 when the caustic circulation was continuing in the solvent extraction plant, operator Shri Pradip Kushwah observed choking in the 18.cri.wp.486.2023judgment.odt evaporator pipeline through the glass flow meter provided on the pipeline. He moved this pipe in up and down direction multiple times to give external water pressure to clear the choking. It is alleged that suddenly within 10 minutes, when the chocking was cleared, the hot caustic solution came down with pressure and came out through the open glass flow meter and splashed over on operator Shri Pradip Kushwah and assistant operator Shri Vijaykumar Rajput, who were standing in front of the glass flow meter. They sustained burn injuries. They succumbed to the burn injuries. The shift incharge immediately informed the Manager. It is stated that by 18.cri.wp.486.2023judgment.odt undertaking the process of clearing the choking, the risk was invited. There were likely chances of the workers coming into contact with hot chemicals. Proper protective equipments were not provided. Learned CJM vide order dated 10.11.2021 made over the complaint to the Court of Judicial Magistrate First Class-2, Washim. Learned JMFC-2, Washim on 10.11.2021 passed the order of issuance of summons to the accused. The 18.cri.wp.486.2023judgment.odt",
    "facts": "3 The petitioner has been facing the prosecution in a complaint case under Section 7A(2)(a) read with Section 92 of the Factories Act, 1948 (For short ' the Factories Act'). It is stated that this amounts to a contravention of the provisions of Section 7A(2) Ram Bharat vs State Of Mah. Thr. M.N. Ratnaparkhi on 1 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/153510493/ 2 (a) of the Factories Act. 4",
    "arguments": "Learned Advocate for the petitioner however confined his arguments to the only ground namely that the order of issuance of a process is mechanical order inasmuch as it does not reflect the application of mind. It is further stated that the learned Magistrate has not recorded his prima facie satisfaction about the offences made out and the reasons for the same. In support of this submission, the learned Advocate has placed reliance on the decision in the case of Lalankumar Singh and others .v"
  },
